{"repositoryId":199712643,"availability":"available","full":"wyeworks/elixir_console","name":"elixir_console","description":"Elixir Web Console","category":"Other","language":"Elixir","stars":80,"forks":9,"created":"2019-07-30T19:13:46Z","updated":"2023-05-22T18:49:07Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://elixirconsole.wyeworks.com/","topics":["elixir","hacktoberfest"],"demo":"https://play.rust-lang.org/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:46.008Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:46.008Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:46.008Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T17:01:46.008Z","stars":80,"forks":9}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["This project is inspired in existing playground sites from distinct communities, such as SwiftPlayground and Rust Playground, yet, it is unique because it aims to mimic the Elixir interactive shell (iEX).","This project was initially implemented to participate in the Phoenix Phrenzy contest. It is an example of the capabilities of Phoenix and LiveView.","Beyond its primary purpose, this is a research initiative. We are exploring the implications of executing untrusted Elixir code in a sandboxed manner. In particular, we want to solve it without using extra infrastructure, being as accessible and easy to use as possible. We have plans to create a package that includes the sandbox functionality. This package would enable the usage of Elixir as a scripting language (although we are not sure if this is a good idea)."],"features":["Bindings are persisted through the current session. Users can assign values to variables. They will remain visible at the side of the screen.","Pressing the Tab key displays a list of suggestions based on what the user is currently typing in the command input. If only one option is available, the word is autocompleted. It will help to discover modules and…","The console presents the history of executed commands and results. The sidebar will display the documentation of Elixir functions when the user clicks on them.","There is easy access to already-executed commands pressing Up and Down keys when the focus is in the command input."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/wyeworks/elixir_console/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"ba5b148cc193bc9008a2ffc8642e837cde41e883480731221ca5a67d87746ac8","extractedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:46.133Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:46.133Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"This project is inspired in existing playground sites from distinct communities, such as SwiftPlayground and Rust Playground, yet, it is unique because it aims to mimic the Elixir interactive shell (iEX).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/wyeworks/elixir_console/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"ba5b148cc193bc9008a2ffc8642e837cde41e883480731221ca5a67d87746ac8","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/wyeworks/elixir_console/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:46.134Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2023-05-22T18:49:07Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/wyeworks/elixir_console/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-15T17:01:46.134Z","hash":"ba5b148cc193bc9008a2ffc8642e837cde41e883480731221ca5a67d87746ac8","originalBytes":9539,"storedBytes":9539,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["elixir","console","code","web","functions","atoms","modules","security","server","number","project","code.","command","does","existing","system","user","when","would","about","additional","due","execution","issue","language","limited","list","other","providing","run","some","usage","users","access","because","currently","executed","functionality","invocations","limitations","only","people","playground","problem","process","processes.","safe","sandbox","section","see","send","solution","thanks","time","whitelist","allow","any","atom","attempt","available","backend","before","being","both","capabilities",